    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d637">

                <pb facs="0884" n="770" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg770"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1490: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Paraguayan Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Zubizarreta</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State and the
                            Diplomatic Representatives of the American Republics in
                            Washington</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-22">October 22, 1931</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:30
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>My Government thanks you for the concern and friendly interest shown in the
                    cablegram which I had the honor to receive, and which coincides with its desire
                    for peace and aspirations for harmony. My Government is confident that the
                    approaching conferences for the study of a pact of nonaggression will permit of
                    considering in a spirit of justice the controlling reasons for the present
                    situation in the Chaco, and that it will be possible to arrive at such an
                    agreement on the basis of the recognition of and respect for the rights of my
                    country and of the juridical regime disturbed by the present military occupation
                    by Bolivia.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Geronimo
                    Zubizarreta</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[The inaugural meeting between the delegates of Bolivia and Paraguay to
                        discuss a nonaggression pact was held at the Pan American Union on November
                        11. The delegates of Bolivia not having arrived at that time, it was agreed
                        that the Assistant Secretary of State, Mr. Francis White, should call
                        another meeting of the neutral representatives <pb facs="0885" n="771"
                            xml:id="pg771"/> and the delegates of Bolivia and Paraguay. The date
                        selected was November 24. (724.3415/1563b, 1581)]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
